    "created_at": "2022-05-26T05:23:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-26T05:23:34Z",
    "body": "> If I recall correctly, iPad changed to report desktop UAs with the introduction of iPadOS. I haven't checked with 12.9\" Pro and 10.2\". But I guess non-mini iPads report desktop-ish strings by default...?\r\n\r\nIIRC, there's no difference between explicitly requesting a desktop site on iOS and the desktop default on larger iPadOS devices.\r\n\r\n> the OS version after Mac OS X on larger iPads is 10_15_6, not 10_15_7 that is what Safari on macOS reports\r\n\r\nYeah, Safari on macOS originally had it capped to 10_15_6 on macOS 11+, but then this was changed to 10_15_7 when macOS 10.15.7 shipped; apparently desktop-mode iOS/iPadOS never changed, which I've occasionally thought I ought to fix, but haven't.\r\n\r\n> Mostly curious about the \"Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1\" bit at the end.\r\n\r\n15E148 is also a constant (which seems to be a build number [slightly before iOS 11.3](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IOS_11#History)).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
